# Eviction Data Import Rules

## CSV Import Guidelines
- Use pandas for CSV file processing
- Handle date formats consistently (MM/DD/YYYY)
- Process imports in batches of 100 records
- Log all import operations
- Validate data before import

## Data Cleaning Rules
- Remove leading/trailing whitespace from text fields
- Standardize county names
- Parse case numbers consistently
- Extract plaintiff and defendant names from case descriptions
- Handle missing values appropriately

## Security Guidelines
- Never store raw passwords or sensitive data
- Anonymize tenant information where possible
- Keep audit trail of all data imports
- Validate file permissions before processing

## Database Operations
- Use SQLAlchemy for all database operations
- Implement proper error handling and rollbacks
- Maintain data integrity constraints
- Use batch processing for large imports

## Code Structure
```python
# Standard import pattern
import pandas as pd
from datetime import datetime
from models import db, EvictionRecord

def import_eviction_data(csv_path):
    """Import eviction data from CSV file"""
    # Validation
    validate_file(csv_path)
    
    # Data processing
    df = pd.read_csv(csv_path)
    clean_data(df)
    
    # Batch import
    with db.session.begin():
        process_in_batches(df)
```

## Error Handling
- Log all errors with stack traces
- Implement retry logic for failed imports
- Maintain transaction integrity
- Provide detailed error messages

## Reporting
- Generate import summary reports
- Track success/failure rates
- Monitor data quality metrics
- Report any anomalies 